    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0979" n="885" xml:id="pg885"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-08-11"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Aug. 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 943.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information a copy of my note, No. 135, of this date, to the minister of foreign
                    affairs, regarding spoliations at Harpoot, which I trust will meet your
                    approval. A simple announcement of the unsatisfactory character of the note of
                    the foreign minister seemed to be most proper at present.</p>
                <p>The detention of the wives of naturalized Americans and the imprisonment of our
                    citizens at Aleppo have engrossed my attention recently, but a longer delay in
                    making known your opinion of the foreign minister’s note was not deemed
                    proper.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d839-a1.xml" xpointer="d839-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
